        "stop_reason": {
          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "I've completed the INI parser. Here's what was built and verified.\n\n## Implementation\n\nSix implementation files in the root package, layered by responsibility:\n\n| File | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| [ini.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\ini.mbt) | public `parse` entry point |\n| [ini_error.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\ini_error.mbt) | `IniParseError` suberror + `malformed` helper (reports the 1-based line) |\n| [ini_scanner.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\ini_scanner.mbt) | line splitting (LF/CRLF, no phantom line after a final break), separator search, inline-comment cut, trailing-backslash run, control-char check |\n| [ini_value.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\ini_value.mbt) | the three carriers, the per-carrier escape table, continuation |\n| [ini_parser.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\ini_parser.mbt) | single-pass document assembly, section re-opening, key validation |\n| [ini_printer.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\ini_printer.mbt) | `print`, written against the grammar rather than the parser |\n\nKey decisions: input stays `StringView` slices (copied only for decoded values and map keys); continuation is decided on the undecoded line by counting the trailing backslash run (odd = marker, even = literals), which is the only way `k=a\\\\` (value `a\\`) stays distinguishable from `k=a\\`; values print as double-quoted literals so whitespace, `;`, `#`, `=` and `:` need no special handling; a leading UTF-8 BOM is dropped.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `moon test` → **44/44 pass** (12 public + 32 added). Added suites: [ini_dialect_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\ini_dialect_test.mbt) (one test per `specs/ini.md` rule, including the four continuation run lengths, all three escape tables, CRLF, invalid forms) and [ini_property_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\ini_property_test.mbt) (round trip, no-panic fuzzing, print/parse idempotence table). Also ran the properties at 20 000 cases each during development.\n- `moon check` → 0 errors, **0 diagnostics from the files I wrote** (the 7 remaining warnings all originate in the pristine template files and `moon.pkg`).\n- `moon build --target wasm-gc`, `moon info` → clean; `pkg.generated.mbti` regenerated.\n- An independent conformance audit found no functional deviation; its two actionable items (BOM handling, a wrong line number in the dangling-continuation message) are fixed and covered by tests.\n- `ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt` and `ini_pub_test.mbt` are **byte-identical** to the pristine template (`diff` clean against `git show HEAD:tasks/ini/…`). Note: running `moon fmt` rewrites those template files (`derive(...)` → `#derive(...)`, `Int` → `Int32`) — I reverted that each time, so `moon fmt --check` still flags exactly those two files; every file I authored is formatter-clean.\n\nDocumentation is in [README.md](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\README.md) (architecture, rule-by-rule behavior, usage, testing, design rationale)."
        }
