          "message": "The INI parser is complete and the whole suite is green.\n\n## What was built\n\nA real scanner/parser/printer (no fixture special-casing), one responsibility per file:\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| [ini.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_2/ini.mbt) | `pub fn parse` entry point |\n| [ini_lines.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_2/ini_lines.mbt) | code-unit constants, trimming, LF/CRLF line splitting, continuation-marker detection |\n| [ini_value.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_2/ini_value.mbt) | escape table, inline comments, quoted/unquoted values, continuation joining |\n| [ini_section.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_2/ini_section.mbt) | `[name]` headers and the wrapped-quote rule |\n| [ini_key.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_2/ini_key.mbt) | key trimming/validation (no control characters) |\n| [ini_parser.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_2/ini_parser.mbt) | line classification, entry parsing, `Doc` assembly |\n| [ini_print.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_2/ini_print.mbt) | `pub fn print` (always double-quoted, sorted) |\n\nKey semantics: first `=`/`:` wins; quoted carriers close only on their own line with escape-aware scanning; each carrier decodes its own escape set and keeps unknown sequences verbatim; continuation is decided on the raw line by the parity of the trailing backslash run; continuation lines contribute text, not syntax; repeated headers re-open and duplicate keys are last-wins.\n\nThree real bugs were found and fixed during development: `StringView::get_char` returns `None` at a surrogate-pair midpoint (so all scanning now uses code units), a trailing newline no longer invents an empty line (so `key=value\\` at EOF raises), and continuation-derived text no longer gets its comment markers stripped.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `moon check`: 0 errors, and **no