          "message": "The implementation is complete and validated. Here's the summary:\n\n## What I built\n\nA real INI parser/printer in the root `ini` package, split by responsibility:\n\n| file | role |\n| --- | --- |\n| [scanner.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\scanner.mbt) | character classes, LF/CRLF line splitting, trimming, backslash-run counting |\n| [value_parser.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\value_parser.mbt) | the three carriers (`Raw`, `DoubleQuoted`, `SingleQuoted`), escape table, blank-gated inline comments, `\\`-continuation |\n| [parser.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\parser.mbt) | `parse`: line classification, section headers, first-`=`/`:` entries, last-wins duplicates, section re-opening |\n| [printer.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\printer.mbt) | `print`: double-quoted values with escapes, safe section-header rendering |\n| [errors.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\errors.mbt) | `IniParseError`, messages naming the 1-based line |\n\nKey rules implemented from `specs/ini.md`: line-based section recognition (`[a]` name trimming, one wrapping quote pair stripped, brackets rejected, trailing blanks/comment only), first `=`/`:` as separator (so URLs keep everything), control-character/empty-key rejection, quoted values closing on their own line with only blanks/comment after, the exact escape table per carrier, and continuation decided on the **raw** line by counting trailing backslashes (odd = marker, even = escaped literals), joined directly with the pre-marker blanks kept.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `moon test`: **62/62 pass** — the 12 public cases (including both property tests) plus 50 spec-derived cases I added in [ini_dialect_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_dialect_test.mbt), [ini_value_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_value_test.mbt), [ini_error_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_error_test.mbt), [ini_print_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_print_test.mbt) (escape/continuation tables, CRLF, real-world git-config/systemd/php.ini/Windows-INNI shapes, every rejection condition, 1000 generated round trips, 1000 random-text no-panic runs).\n- `moon check`: 0 errors; the only remaining warnings (7) all originate in the protected files (`ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt`, `ini_pub_test.mbt`, `moon.pkg`). My files and tests are warning-free and `moon fmt`-clean.\n- `moon info` regenerated [pkg.generated.mbti](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\pkg.generated.mbti) (`parse`, `print`, `Doc`, `IniParseError`).\n- I restored `ini_spec.mbt` and `ini_qc.mbt` byte-for-byte after `moon fmt`'s deprecated-syntax migration rewrote them (verified: `} derive(Eq, Debug)` and `min~ : Int` back in place), so the protected fixtures are untouched.\n- An independent audit (`@builtin/review.mbtx`) found no blockers; I acted on its notes by documenting the printer's key-spelling limitation and labelling the two deliberately liberal test assertions.\n\nDocumentation lives in [README.md](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\README.md) (architecture, algorithms, escape table, usage, testing, design rationale) with a short module readme in `README.mbt.md`."
